Meaning of the word

Yamah — Yamaraj; Tu — without doubt; Kalnabhena — from Kalnab; Vishwakarma — Vishwakarma; Mayena — from Maya; Vai — without doubt; Shambharah —
Shambhar; Yuyudhe — fought; Twashtra — from Twashta; Savitra — from Suryadev; Tu — without doubt; Virochanah — Virochana Asura..

From Yamraj Kalnabh, from Vishwakarma Maya Danav, from Twashta Shambhar, and from Suryadev Virochana
Started fighting. Aparajitena, the son of Namuchirashwa, the son of Vrishaparvana. The sun, the best of gods, is the best among thousands of arrows. 30>. Rahu and Soma, Pulomana, and Yuyudheenila. Nishumbhasya Devi Bhadrakali Tarasvini. 31. Meaning of the word

Aparajitan—From the invincible deity; Namuchi—Namuchi Asura; Ashwinau—The Ashwini Kumaras; Vrishaparvana—With Vrishaparva Daitya;
Suryah—The Sun God; Bali-Sutaih—With the sons of Bali; Devah—The deities; Baan-Jyeshtaah—Among whom Baan is prominent; Shaten—One hundred;
Cha—And; Rahunah—From Rahu; Cha—Also; Tatha—And; Somah—The Moon God; Pulomana—With Puloma; Yuyudhe—Warred;
Anilah—the wind god; Nishumbhah—the demon Nishumbha; Shumbhayoh—with Shumbha; Devi—the goddess Durga; Bhadrakali—Bhadrakali;
Tarasvini—extremely powerful. The invincible deity fought with Namuchi Asura and both Ashwini Kumaras with Vrishaparva.
War was fought. The Sun God, Maharaj, clashed with the hundred sons of Bali, among whom Bana was prominent. Chandradeva fought with Rahu. Vayudev fought with Puloma and Shumbh and Nishumbh, who were extremely powerful Maya.
They fought with Durgadevi named Bhadrakali. Vrishakapitas tu jambhena mahishena vibhavasuha. Ilvāla: with the wind, the son of Vāyu, the fire. 32). Kamadeva, the auspicious, the terrible, and the mother. Brihaspatishochanasana narakena shancharah. 33). Maruti Nivatakavachah, Kaleyai Ravaso Arama.
Vishwadeva, the Rudras, are with Paula, the fierce one. 34). Meaning of the word

Vrishakapi: Shiva; Tu: without doubt; Jambhen: with Jambha; Mahishena: from Mahishasura; Vibhavasuha: Agni Deva; Ilvala:
Ilvala Asura; Saha Vatapiha: with his brother Vatapi; Brahma-putraha: with the sons of Brahma, as with Vashistha; Arim-dam: Hey
The destroyer of enemies, Maharaj Parikshit; Kamdevena - from Kamadeva; Durmarshah - Durmarsha; Utkalah - Utkala's; Matrubhisah - with mothers;
With the goddesses named; Brihaspatih - from Brihaspati; Cha - and; Ushnasah - from Shukracharya; Narakena - from Narakasura;
Shanaiashcharah - from Shani; Marutah - from Vayu; Nivatakavachaih - from Nivatakavacha Asura; Kalayaih - from Kalakeya; Vasavah
Amrah - Vasus fought; Vishvedevah - from Vishvedevas; Tu - without doubt; Paulomaih - with Paulomas; Rudrah - from eleven Rudras;
Krodhavashah - with the demons in anger.
